Read or restore a task's specification history. Every material edit to a task appends an immutable revision, so an overwritten description is recoverable. `list` summarises revisions newest first with author, source, and edit summary. `get` reads one revision whole. `diff` shows which fields changed between two revisions, defaulting the second to the current version — the fastest way to answer "what did that edit actually change". `restore` puts the task back to a revision by appending a new one; earlier revisions are never modified or erased, and the restore is subject to the same status-transition and dependency rules as any other edit. Read the diff before restoring, and say why in `edit_summary`.
